nt":"Email authentication works through DNS records that prove you authorized NorthRelay to send email on behalf of your domain. Receiving mail servers check these records to verify legitimacy."},"6779":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-33","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"Record"},"6780":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-34","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"Purpose"},"6781":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-35","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"Required"},"6782":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-36","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"**SPF**"},"6783":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-37","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"Declares which servers are allowed to send email for your domain"},"6784":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-38","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"Yes"},"6785":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-39","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"**DKIM**"},"6786":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-40","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"Adds a cryptographic signature to prove the email was not tampered with"},"6787":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-41","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"Yes (auto-configured)"},"6788":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-42","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"**DMARC**"},"6789":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-43","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"Tells receiving servers what to do with emails that fail SPF/DKIM checks"},"6790":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-44","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"Strongly recommended"},"6791":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-45","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"**MX**"},"6792":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-46","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"Routes inbound email to NorthRelay's mailbox servers (inbox users only)"},"6793":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-47","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"Only for inbox"},"6794":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-48","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#spf-record","content":"SPF (Sender Policy Framework) tells receiving mail servers which IP addresses are authorized to send email for your domain."},"6795":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-49","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"Add a TXT record at the root of your domain:"},"6796":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-50","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"Field"},"6797":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-51","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"Value"},"6798":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-52","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"**Type**"},"6799":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-53","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"TXT"},"6800":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-54","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"**Host/Name**"},"6801":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-55","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"`@` (or leave blank, depending on your DNS provider)"},"6802":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-56","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"**Value**"},"6803":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-57","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"`v=spf1 include:_spf.north-pipe.ca -all`"},"6804":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-58","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"**TTL**"},"6805":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-59","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"3600 (or default)"},"6806":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-60","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#how-it-works","content":"The `include:_spf.north-pipe.ca` directive tells receiving servers to look up NorthRelay's SPF record, which lists all NorthRelay sending IPs (both shared and sovereign relay servers, IPv4 and IPv6). The `-all` suffix means \"reject email from any other source\" — this is the strictest and most secure setting."},"6807":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-61","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#if-you-already-have-an-spf-record","content":"A domain can only have **one** SPF TXT record. If you already send email through another provider, merge the records:"},"6808":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-62","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#if-you-already-have-an-spf-record","content":"Do not create a second TXT record starting with `v=spf1` — this will cause SPF to fail entirely."},"6809":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-63","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#common-mistakes","content":"Using `~all` (softfail) instead of `-all` (hardfail) — softfail is weaker and may not protect you"},"6810":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-64","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#common-mistakes","content":"Adding more than 10 DNS lookups in your SPF chain (SPF has a 10-lookup limit)"},"6811":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-65","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#common-mistakes","content":"Creating multiple SPF records on the same domain"},"6812":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-66","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dkim-record","content":"DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail) adds a cryptographic signature to each outgoing email, allowing the recipient to verify the message was not altered in transit."},"6813":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-67","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"DKIM is **automatically configured** when you verify your domain in the NorthRelay dashboard. After verification, NorthRelay publishes the DKIM public key and signs all outgoing email from your domain."},"6814":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-68","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"To verify your domain:"},"6815":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-69","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"Go to **Dashboard → Domains**"},"6816":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-70","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"Click **Add Domain** and enter your domain name"},"6817":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-71","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"Add the verification TXT record shown in the dashboard to your DNS"},"6818":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-72","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"Click **Verify**"},"6819":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-73","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#auto-configured","content":"Once verified, DKIM signing is enabled automatically"},"6820":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-74","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#verifying-dkim","content":"After domain verification, confirm the DKIM record is published:"},"6821":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-75","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#verifying-dkim","content":"You should see a response containing a `v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=...` value. If the record is missing, wait up to 48 hours for DNS propagation, then check again."},"6822":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-76","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#subdomains","content":"DKIM signing supports subdomains automatically. If you send from `notifications@sub.yourdomain.com`, the parent domain's DKIM key will sign the email (using the `SubDomains=yes` configuration on NorthRelay's signing infrastructure)."},"6823":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-77","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dmarc-record","content":"DMARC (Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting, and Conformance) tells receiving servers how to handle emails that fail SPF or DKIM checks, and where to send aggregate reports."},"6824":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-78","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"Add a TXT record at `_dmarc.yourdomain.com`:"},"6825":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-79","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"Field"},"6826":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-80","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"Value"},"6827":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-81","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"**Type**"},"6828":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-82","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"TXT"},"6829":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-83","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"**Host/Name**"},"6830":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-84","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"`_dmarc`"},"6831":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-85","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"**Value**"},"6832":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-86","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"`v=DMARC1; p=quarantine; rua=mailto:dmarc@yourdomain.com`"},"6833":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-87","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"**TTL**"},"6834":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-88","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"3600 (or default)"},"6835":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-89","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":